<title>DENMARK: Maersk open new Mauritius route.</title>
<headline>Maersk open new Mauritius route.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maersk Line, owned by Danish shipping and energy group A.P. Moeller, said on Wednesday it planned to open a new container vessel route from South Africa to Mauritius starting on June 17.</p>
<p>Maersk said in a statement that the new two-weekly service would be operated by a ship with capacity for 125 twenty-foot containers.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
